        "import polars as pl\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from lets_plot import *\n",
        "\n",
        "LetsPlot.setup_html(isolated_frame=True)"
      ],
      "id": "665d61f7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Learn morea about Code Cells: https://quarto.org/docs/reference/cells/cells-jupyter.html\n",
        "\n",
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "df = pl.read_csv(\"names_year_csv.csv\")"
      ],
      "id": "9d1a4183",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 1\n",
        "\n",
        "__What was the earliest year that the name ‘Felisha’ was used?__\n",
        "\n",
        "The earliest recorded year that \"Felisha\" appeared was in 1964.\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "424831c8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Q1\n",
        "\n",
        "df.filter(pl.col(\"name\") == \"Felisha\").select(\"year\").min()"
      ],
      "id": "59717636",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 2\n",
        "\n",
        "__What year had the most babies named 'David'? How many babies were named 'David' that year?__\n",
        "\n",
        "The most babies that were named \"David\" in one year 86389, and that was in 1955.\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "88146faa"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Q2\n",
        "\n",
        "df.filter(pl.col(\"name\") == \"David\").sort(\"Total\", descending=True).head(1)"
      ],
      "id": "8bfaafe1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 3\n",
        "\n",
        "__What year did your name hit its peak? How many babies were named your name in that year?__\n",
        "\n",
        "In 2012, there were 24 babies named Rayce.\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "36e617be"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Q3\n",
        "df.filter(pl.col(\"name\") == \"Rayce\").sort(\"Total\", descending=True).head(1)"
      ],
      "id": "e05e6044",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 4\n",
        "\n",
        "__In the most recent year, what was the most common female name in Utah?__ \n",
        "\n",
        "The most common female name in Utah, in the latest recorded year (2024), was Olivia, with 14718 results.\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "200267ca"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Q5\n",
        "df.filter(pl.col(\"year\") == pl.col(\"year\").max()).sort(\"UT\", descending=True).head(10)"
      ],
